        <p class="pex">There is a political space the Black Lives Matter movement quietly recognized that never appeared on any organizing chart: the barbershop chair. The barbershop and its neighborhood cousins were where the arguments that the marches carried w…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@albacorerye</span></span>Upholstery hides a frame that has to be sound, and the first job is never the fabric. Anyone can recover a chair; the work is checking the joints, tightening what time ha</div>
